WEBVTT

00:00:10.139 --> 00:00:12.099
This is starting to get out of control.

00:00:12.141 --> 00:00:13.433
No, no, this is perfect.

00:00:13.475 --> 00:00:14.684
Remember your training.

00:00:14.726 --> 00:00:16.228
Wait, did we train for this?

00:00:19.773 --> 00:00:21.108
[rabbits] Whoa!

00:00:24.278 --> 00:00:25.279
[grunting]

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:30.366
How is this perfect?

00:00:30.408 --> 00:00:32.202
She should've heard us by now.

00:00:32.244 --> 00:00:34.579
[pop song playing on speaker] ♪ This is my fight song ♪

00:00:34.621 --> 00:00:37.291
♪ Take back my life song ♪

00:00:37.332 --> 00:00:39.459
♪ Prove I'm all right song ♪

00:00:42.879 --> 00:00:44.298
[Mopsy groans]

00:00:44.339 --> 00:00:45.381
I'm hit.

00:00:45.423 --> 00:00:47.259
-I'm hit. -Mopsy!

00:00:47.301 --> 00:00:48.343
No!

00:00:48.384 --> 00:00:49.385
[yelling]

00:00:52.681 --> 00:00:55.184
Flopsy, I need you to know something.

00:00:55.225 --> 00:00:56.559
I'm not the oldest.

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:59.688
so cute and lovable. -You were always -What?

00:00:59.729 --> 00:01:01.606
And Cotton-Tail, well, she's--

00:01:01.648 --> 00:01:02.899
[war cry]

00:01:04.776 --> 00:01:05.777
[yelling]

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:07.570
Cotton-Tail,

00:01:07.612 --> 00:01:10.365
so Mom and Dad told us I was the oldest,

00:01:10.406 --> 00:01:11.992
so I had something.

00:01:12.034 --> 00:01:14.203
you're the oldest, But, really,

00:01:14.244 --> 00:01:16.330
and I'm nothing.

00:01:16.371 --> 00:01:18.498
No! Mopsy, don't go.

00:01:19.082 --> 00:01:20.083
Mopsy?

00:01:20.583 --> 00:01:21.960
[Flopsy sobbing]

00:01:24.546 --> 00:01:25.839
[sniffing]

00:01:25.881 --> 00:01:28.925
Hmm? It was just a tomato. I'm fine.

00:01:28.967 --> 00:01:30.719
Guys, I'm fine!

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:32.929
It's just a tomato!

00:01:32.971 --> 00:01:35.224
any of that stuff, got me? Hey, you never heard

00:01:35.265 --> 00:01:36.308
Hmm.

00:01:37.517 --> 00:01:38.685
Dink.

00:01:38.727 --> 00:01:40.229
[ominous music continues]

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.829
♪ Fight left in me ♪

00:01:57.871 --> 00:01:59.164
[Peter gasps]

00:02:00.082 --> 00:02:01.958
Gotcha! You listen to me.

00:02:02.709 --> 00:02:05.170
I am not a bad guy.

00:02:05.212 --> 00:02:06.380
You turned me into this.

00:02:06.421 --> 00:02:08.382
I am a nice person.

00:02:08.423 --> 00:02:10.508
I've chilled out, man.

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:12.052
I'm cool now.

00:02:12.094 --> 00:02:15.513
I've evolved, but you, you're still the same.

00:02:15.555 --> 00:02:17.766
Still full of mischief.

00:02:17.807 --> 00:02:21.353
And that's why things are not going to end well for you.

00:02:21.395 --> 00:02:25.399
Because you poked at me and you poked at me,

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:28.610
for me to do is wring your-- until all that's left

00:02:28.651 --> 00:02:29.778
What's going on here?

00:02:29.819 --> 00:02:31.947
You've got to chew your food!

00:02:31.988 --> 00:02:33.531
I saved him.

00:02:33.573 --> 00:02:34.991
What happened? Is he okay?

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:36.368
Yeah, I... He...

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:38.620
he was choking on some radish. The poor little guy,

00:02:38.661 --> 00:02:40.705
I've checked his pulse, So I just...

00:02:40.747 --> 00:02:42.332
and everything's gonna be okay.

00:02:42.374 --> 00:02:44.793
You're going to be okay!

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:47.796
So off you go. Off you go. There we are.

00:02:47.837 --> 00:02:49.172
[Thomas sighs]

00:02:49.881 --> 00:02:50.882
It's a miracle.

00:02:51.383 --> 00:02:52.426
Yeah.

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:54.719
I thought I heard some loud noises.

00:02:54.761 --> 00:02:56.054
It was a bit of a ruckus.

00:02:56.096 --> 00:02:58.098
I was painting, so I can't be sure, but did you--

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:00.642
No, I don't think so... I was weeding.

00:03:00.683 --> 00:03:04.146
I do make grunting noises when I weed sometimes. [grunts]

00:03:04.187 --> 00:03:06.815
It's just people have used explosives before to keep the rabbits out.

00:03:06.856 --> 00:03:07.899
Explosives?

00:03:07.941 --> 00:03:08.984
But you wouldn't do that.

00:03:09.025 --> 00:03:10.110
something like that. I wouldn't do

00:03:10.152 --> 00:03:11.403
-No, of course not. -They're angels.

00:03:11.445 --> 00:03:12.612
This is their place as much as ours.

00:03:12.654 --> 00:03:14.572
-Learned that from you. -Yeah, exactly.

00:03:14.614 --> 00:03:16.950
I just thought I heard something.

00:03:16.992 --> 00:03:19.369
flying bird up there? Is that a two-winged

00:03:19.411 --> 00:03:20.662
-I must mark it down. -Where?

00:03:20.703 --> 00:03:22.289
-She believes him. -Up there.

00:03:22.331 --> 00:03:23.873
get rid of him now. We'll never

00:03:23.915 --> 00:03:25.625
[Bea] I don't think so.

00:03:25.667 --> 00:03:28.503
that... In the faraway tree. [Thomas] Up there. Just in

00:03:30.546 --> 00:03:31.547
[Bea gasps]

00:03:33.425 --> 00:03:35.177
You are using explosives.

00:03:36.219 --> 00:03:37.595
You lied to me.

00:03:37.637 --> 00:03:38.847
-Well, yes, but-- -[explosion]

00:03:43.268 --> 00:03:44.269
[all gasp]

00:03:49.107 --> 00:03:50.192
[gasps]

00:04:03.579 --> 00:04:04.580
-[crashing] -Oh!

00:04:07.917 --> 00:04:09.127
Oh...

00:04:09.169 --> 00:04:10.170
My house.

00:04:10.962 --> 00:04:11.963
My paintings.

00:04:14.674 --> 00:04:15.675
Their burrow.

00:04:18.345 --> 00:04:20.096
This is going to be difficult for you to hear,

00:04:21.556 --> 00:04:22.557
but he did it.

00:04:23.099 --> 00:04:24.184
He detonated it.

00:04:25.935 --> 00:04:26.936
He's a rabbit.

00:04:27.562 --> 00:04:28.563
I know.

00:04:29.189 --> 00:04:30.606
But somehow,

00:04:30.648 --> 00:04:33.026
he found the detonator, and he took his paw...

00:04:34.277 --> 00:04:36.405
And he did all that to come between us.

00:04:36.446 --> 00:04:38.031
He's a rabbit!

00:04:38.073 --> 00:04:39.782
Let's be reasonable. All right. Okay.

00:04:39.824 --> 00:04:41.743
they rob from the garden. For a start, you know

00:04:41.784 --> 00:04:44.871
they set traps in my bed? Did you know

00:04:44.913 --> 00:04:47.207
I hurt my little fingers! So when I woke up,

00:04:47.249 --> 00:04:49.125
electricity against me, And then they used

00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:50.544
which we invented,

00:04:50.585 --> 00:04:53.255
their own nefarious purposes! but they modified for

00:04:53.296 --> 00:04:54.923
And they saw the Bananagrams,

00:04:54.964 --> 00:04:57.509
they saw the walk in the park. they saw the bicycle ride,

00:04:57.551 --> 00:04:59.761
the jackets? We don't know! And where did they get

00:04:59.802 --> 00:05:01.430
been there all along. But they've

00:05:01.471 --> 00:05:03.598
You're a crazy person.

00:05:03.639 --> 00:05:05.683
I thought I liked you. I can't believe

00:05:06.601 --> 00:05:07.602
You do like me.

00:05:10.272 --> 00:05:11.565
And I like you. That's...

00:05:12.899 --> 00:05:14.817
Are you okay, sweeties?

00:05:14.859 --> 00:05:15.818
I'm sorry.

00:05:18.572 --> 00:05:19.781
Come on.

00:05:19.822 --> 00:05:22.075
from this evil man. Let's get away

00:05:29.832 --> 00:05:30.875
I'm sorry.

00:05:30.917 --> 00:05:33.044
Yes, so am I.

00:05:40.218 --> 00:05:41.303
[sighs]

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:51.104
[chicks] Another day? I can't believe it!

00:05:51.146 --> 00:05:52.439
-This is so exciting! -[excited chatter]

00:05:52.481 --> 00:05:53.689
I know, right?

00:05:53.731 --> 00:05:55.484
Can you believe it?

00:05:55.525 --> 00:05:58.403
Although, things aren't going so great now,

00:05:58.445 --> 00:06:00.655
so maybe last night should've been it!

